## The Goal: Build a Repeatable Workflow

Our project's main goal was to develop a platform for biologists that the technological team could continue to expand and customize after handoff. 

That being said, the project needed to accomplish some indispensable functions:

- it needed to accept project-specific information from the user, such as a project boundary/footprint. 
- Upon reception of the project boundary, the app would have to query the relevant species datasets (CNPS and CNDDB).
- Next, the returned records would have to be processed and organized. Biologists wanted to be able to view the raw results based on the dataset.
- The plaform had to allow users to explore results spatially and analytically. The results would display the radius of occurrence of plants and animals in a map as well as show ordered charts of the number of occurrences for each species found within the project. 
- Lastly, it needed to produce outputs that could be used in regulatory reporting. The returned records needed to be formatted in a report-friendly format in conformity with CEQA regulations. 

