## Challenges & Design Decisions

- we decided for users to define their search area with one type of file and to only take in one project area at a time. 
- we decided to make the app in-session rather than be able to store previous project information.
- the search radius was handled differently depending on the user input by giving them choices depending on the regulatory req (5-mile, 9-quad)
- in the report, we decided to match the actual pto report they typically use for reporting in style and categorizing different species categories (plants & lichens, birds, reptiles, amphibians, fish etc.)
- to make the workflow easier for someone who doesn't want to interact with Python directly we wrapped it into a Streamlit app that is deployed by docker.

Example: One design challenge was balancing the amount of information available to users with the need to keep the interface manageable. Rather than presenting users with raw query results alone, we organized the output into maps, tables, and summaries that corresponded to different stages of their review process.

