## My Experience: Learned Lessons/ What I Took Away

building a tool for actual users requires thinking beyond just the underlying analysis
- it requires thinking about the overall framework and structure
- you need to foresee potential issues with each feature you develop rather than troubleshoot as you go or implement blindly
- you have to balance what the client wants and what is actually achievable
- user stories make the app clear to understand what goes into it
- some user needs need to be reevaluated in terms of their viability and usability
- you need to be thinking about the long-term evolution of what you are developing: is this just a short-term app meant for quick results in the moment or do we want an app with full customizability that can be expanded and improved long-term?

